🚀 Week 8 – Day 1 Metadata Filtering & Text Splitters 🗂️✂️

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🧠 Introduction

In RAG systems, simply storing embeddings is not enough.

To improve retrieval quality, we use:

* Metadata Filtering
* Text Splitters

These help in:

✔ Better search accuracy
✔ Faster retrieval
✔ More relevant responses

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🗂️ 1. Metadata Filtering

----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 What is Metadata?

```text id="metadata_def"
Additional information stored along with documents or chunks
```

---

📌 Examples of Metadata

* File name
* Page number
* Author
* Source URL
* Document category
* Date created

---

🧾 Example Metadata

```python id="metadata_example"
{
    "source": "policy.pdf",
    "page": 5,
    "department": "HR"
}
```

---

🔍 What is Metadata Filtering?

```text id="metadata_filter_def"
Retrieving documents based on metadata conditions
```

---

📌 Example

Question:

```text id="metadata_question"
"Show HR policies only"
```

Filter:

```python id="metadata_filter_code"
filter = {"department": "HR"}
```

---

🎯 Why Metadata Filtering Matters

✔ Improves retrieval relevance
✔ Reduces search space
✔ Enables document categorization
✔ Supports multi-user systems

---

🧠 Real-World Example

A company chatbot may retrieve:

* HR documents for employees
* Finance documents for accounting team

using metadata filters.

---

💻 Example with ChromaDB

```python id="chroma_filter"
results = collection.query(
    query_texts=["leave policy"],
    where={"department": "HR"}
)
```

---

⚠️ Common Metadata Fields

| Field     | Purpose               |
| --------- | --------------------- |
| source    | Track document origin |
| page      | Identify page number  |
| category  | Group documents       |
| timestamp | Time-based filtering  |

